ALGORITHM JSPRequestFlow

START

1. User enters a JSP URL in the browser.

2. Browser sends an HTTP request to the web server.

3. Web server receives the request.

4. Check whether the JSP page has already been compiled.

5. IF JSP is not compiled THEN
       Translate JSP into a Servlet.
       Compile the Servlet.
   END IF

6. Execute the JSP/Servlet.

7. Retrieve input parameters from the request.

8. Validate the received input.

9. IF input is invalid THEN
       Generate an error message.
       Send error response to the browser.
       STOP
   END IF

10. Call the required backend component.

11. Backend component performs business processing.

12. IF database information is required THEN
        Establish database connection.
        Execute required query.
        Retrieve the result.
        Close database resources.
    END IF

13. Pass the processed data to the JSP.

14. JSP generates dynamic HTML content.

15. Web server creates the HTTP response.

16. Send the response to the browser.

17. Browser displays the generated webpage.

END
